NCBI BLAST nucleotide scoring matrix NUC.4.4 (EDNAFULL)

seqblaze's align matrix "EDNAFULL", also used by the compat presets
emboss-water and emboss-needle, consists of the 225 integer scores of the
NUC.4.4 nucleotide scoring matrix, created by Todd Lowe (12/10/92) and
distributed by NCBI. A generator script transcribed them into compiled
constants. No NCBI file is shipped.

  Source: https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/blast/matrices/NUC.4.4
  Fetched 2026-10-16 (HTTP Last-Modified 1997-08-26); 1,171 bytes;
  sha256 c603e46f9a159fb451632cdf9f9c687bae7daadb30fb2645f5fd09cace707490
  File header: "This matrix was created by Todd Lowe   12/10/92"
  [ncbi-blast-matrices-nuc.4.4]

The file carries no copyright line and no licence statement, so there is no
licence text to reproduce. NCBI's website policies
(https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/home/about/policies/) state that information
created by or for the US government on the site is in the public domain.
Whether the file's author created it for the US government is not verified, so
the file is redistributed as likely, but not certainly, in the public domain (a
judgement, not legal advice). seqblaze credits Todd Lowe and NCBI.

  Source identity: independent agents verified the official file and matching
  local copy on 2026-10-29; the maintainer adopted this evidence on 2026-10-31.
  This records evidence adoption, without a claim of personal inspection.
  The data file has no formal title and no pages. Its identity is the file
  header quoted above (line 2 of the file, after its leading "#"); seqblaze's
  source register records that line, with runs of spaces collapsed, as the
  file's identity. A descriptive citation, not a title printed in the file:
  Lowe, Todd (1992). NCBI BLAST nucleotide scoring matrix file NUC.4.4.
  Distributed by NCBI.

